  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The particle is at rest initially.</p><p>So, the initial velocity&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>The force on the charged particle in the uniform electric field,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Applying the velocity-displacement equation under constant acceleration,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mi>x</mi></math></p>",
